@startuml ProximaDB_Activity_Diagram
!theme aws-orange
title ProximaDB Complete Operation Activity Flow

|Client|
start
:Submit vector operation\n(Insert/Search/Update);

|Network Layer|
:Route to appropriate handler\n(REST/gRPC);
:Parse and validate request;

if (Request valid?) then (yes)
  |Service Layer|
  :Delegate to Vector Service;
  
  if (Operation type?) then (Insert/Update)
    |WAL System|
    :Create WAL entries;
    :Generate batch ID;
    
    |Atomic Operations|
    :Start atomic operation;
    
    |Memtable|
    :Write to WAL memtable;
    :Update content indices;
    :Assign sequences;
    
    if (Immediate sync?) then (yes)
      |Persistence|
      :Serialize to disk;
      :Write WAL file;
    endif
    
    :Commit atomic operation;
    
    |Background Process|
    fork
      :Check memory thresholds;
      
      if (Flush needed?) then (yes)
        |Flush Coordinator|
        :Mark entries for flush;
        :Determine storage engine;
        
        if (Engine type?) then (VIPER)
          |VIPER Engine|
          :Analyze vector clusters;
          :Encode to Parquet;
          :Write clustered files;
        else (LSM)
          |LSM Engine|
          :Create SSTable;
          :Build Bloom filters;
          :Write to Level 0;
        endif
        
        :Complete flush cycle;
        :Clear flushed entries;
      endif
    end fork
    
  else (Search)
    |Search Engine Factory|
    :Create storage-aware engine;
    
    |Multi-Tier Search|
    fork
      |WAL Search|
      :Search unflushed batches;
      :Calculate distances;
    fork again
      |VIPER Search|
      :Apply ML clustering;
      :Search Parquet files;
      :Calculate distances;
    fork again
      |LSM Search|
      :Check Bloom filters;
      :Search SSTables;
      :Calculate distances;
    end fork
    
    |Deduplication|
    :Merge tier results;
    :Remove duplicates by ID;
    :Apply tier priorities;
    :Sort by distance;
    :Limit to k results;
  endif
  
  |Service Layer|
  :Prepare response;
  
else (no)
  |Error Handling|
  :Generate error response;
endif

|Network Layer|
:Serialize response;
:Send to client;

|Client|
:Receive response;
stop

note right : **Key Innovations**\n\n• **Atomic Operations**: Ensures ACID\n  properties with automatic rollback\n\n• **Multi-Tier Search**: 6.10x performance\n  improvement through intelligent routing\n\n• **Background Flush**: Async operation\n  doesn't block client requests\n\n• **ML Clustering**: Optimizes storage\n  layout for query performance

@enduml